<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
     STANDARD SHIPMENT PLUGIN: METHOD SETTINGS (reference)

    Everything a merchant configures per shipping METHOD lives here. Copy this
    file when starting a carrier of your own.

    Two rules that are not negotiable

    1. EVERYTHING GOES INSIDE <fields name="shipmentsparams">. A field declared
       outside it renders, the merchant fills it in, and it is silently
       discarded on save: the value is never seeded back and never written.
       (For a payment plugin the wrapper is "paymentsparams".)

    2. EACH <fieldset> BECOMES A TAB, in the order they appear in this file.
       Give it a `label` language key or the tab falls back to a title-cased
       version of the fieldset name.

    Field types the component provides

    All of them need addfieldprefix="Alfa\Component\Alfa\Administrator\Field",
    which is how Joomla finds the class. Get that wrong and Joomla does NOT
    complain: it silently substitutes a plain text box that validates nothing.

    checkoutfield: pick one of the SHOP'S OWN checkout fields.
        Use it for anything whose column you cannot know: the postcode you
        price by, the phone a courier texts, the country a locker is in.

            <field name="postcode_field" type="checkoutfield"
                   addfieldprefix="Alfa\Component\Alfa\Administrator\Field"
                   types="text" sections="shipping"
                   label="..." description="...">
                <option value="">- Not selected -</option>
            </field>

        types=       restrict to field types: text, tel, country, email, ...
                     ALWAYS restrict. types="tel" is what guarantees the value
                     you read has been validated as a phone number.
        sections=    shipping | billing | registration: which checkout section.
        multiple=    offer several; read them with $cart->delivery()->fields()
                     or ->firstFilled().

        IT SAVES THE FIELD'S ID, NOT THE COLUMN NAME. Renaming a field rewrites
        the name and ALTERs the column; an id does not move. Read it back with
        $cart->delivery()->field($savedId), which resolves the id to a live
        column every time; a deleted field answers "missing", never a stale
        value.

        GIVE EVERY OPTIONAL PICKER AN <option value="">. Without one the first
        matching field is preselected and saved without the merchant touching
        it, which is how a postcode setting came to hold the id of the name
        field. With required="true", leaving it empty is refused by Joomla's own
        validation.

    telephone: a phone number the MERCHANT types, in your own settings.
        Same treatment a customer's number gets at checkout: validated on save
        and stored in E.164 (+306912345678, no spaces, no dashes).

            <field name="contact_phone" type="telephone"
                   addfieldprefix="Alfa\Component\Alfa\Administrator\Field"
                   default_region="GR" require_mobile="0"
                   label="..." description="..."/>

        default_region=   how to read a number typed without a country code.
                          Omit it and the SHOP'S default country is used; if the
                          shop has not set one, a number without a country code
                          is refused rather than guessed at.
        allowed_regions=  comma-separated ISO codes to accept.
        require_mobile=   1 to refuse landlines.
        store_format=     e164 (default) | international | national | rfc3966.
                          Leave it alone. Only e164 is unambiguous; `national`
                          throws the country away and cannot get it back.

        It brings its own filter AND rule, so declaring the type is the whole
        contract. (A filter transforms, a rule accepts or refuses; a rule that
        tries to rewrite a value writes into a copy that is thrown away.)

    categories model="places": pick places (countries, regions, towns).
        See cost-per-place below. Match a delivery against the WHOLE chain with
        $this->placesFor($placeId), never against the id alone: a zone naming a
        country has to match an order going to a town inside it.

    And from Joomla, the ones worth knowing

    subform multiple="true"  repeatable rows (the cost table below).
    sql                      populate a list from a query (payment methods, ...).
    password                 a secret; use it for API keys, never type="text".
    note                     guidance in the form itself, with showon= to make
                             it appear only when it is relevant.
    color, number, radio layout="joomla.form.field.radio.switcher"
    useglobal="true"         inherit a com_alfa global of the SAME field name;
                             Joomla draws "Use Global (...)" and resolves it for
                             you. The names must match; that is how it resolves.
    showon="other_field:1"   show only when another field has a value.

    Reading any of it back

        $method->param('postcode_field')        one value, already decoded
        $method->params()                       all of them

    See ShipmentsPlugin's class docblock for the cart, the destination, the
    pricing primitives and the three error surfaces.
-->
<form>
    <fields name="shipmentsparams">
        <fieldset name="shipmentsparams" label="PLG_ALFA_SHIPMENTS_STANDARD_FIELDSET_SETTINGS">

            <field
                    name="cost-per-place"
                    type="subform"
                    buttons="add,remove,move"
                    hiddenLabel="true"
                    label="All"
                    description=""
                    multiple="true"
            >

                <form>

                    <field name="places"
                           type="categories"
                           model="places"
                           multiple="true"
                           showPath="false"
                           orderBy="id"
                           orderDir="desc"
                           disableDescendants="true"
                           default="0"
                           header="PLG_ALFA_SHIPMENTS_STANDARD_FORM_PLACE_ALL"
                           layout="joomla.form.field.list-fancy-select"
                           label="PLG_ALFA_SHIPMENTS_STANDARD_FORM_CATEGORY_PLACE_LBL">
                      <!--      <option value="0">COM_ALFA_FROM_PLACE_NO_OPTION</option>-->
                    </field>

                    <field
                            name="costs"
                            type="subform"
                            buttons="add,remove,move"
                            class="shrinked-repeatable-table"
                            hiddenLabel="true"
                            label="All"
                            description=""
                            multiple="true"
                            layout="joomla.form.field.subform.repeatable-table"
                    >

                        <form>
                            <field
                                    name="zip-start"
                                    type="text"
                                    default="0"
                                    readonly="false"
                                    label="PLG_ALFA_SHIPMENTS_STANDARD_FORM_SHIPMENT_ZIP_START"
                            />

                            <field
                                    name="zip-end"
                                    type="text"
                                    default="0"
                                    readonly="false"
                                    label="PLG_ALFA_SHIPMENTS_STANDARD_FORM_SHIPMENT_ZIP_END"
                            />

                            <field
                                    name="weight-max"
                                    type="number"
                                    min='0.01'
                                    default="0"
                                    readonly="false"
                                    label="PLG_ALFA_SHIPMENTS_STANDARD_FORM_SHIPMENT_WEIGHT_MAX"
                            />

                            <field
                                    name="width-max"
                                    type="number"
                                    min='0.01'
                                    default="0"
                                    readonly="false"
                                    label="PLG_ALFA_SHIPMENTS_STANDARD_FORM_SHIPMENT_WIDTH_MAX"
                            />

                            <field
                                    name="height-max"
                                    type="number"
                                    min='0.01'
                                    default="0"
                                    readonly="false"
                                    label="PLG_ALFA_SHIPMENTS_STANDARD_FORM_SHIPMENT_HEIGHT_MAX"
                            />

                            <field
                                    name="depth-max"
                                    type="number"
                                    min='0.01'
                                    default="0"
                                    readonly="false"
                                    label="PLG_ALFA_SHIPMENTS_STANDARD_FORM_SHIPMENT_DEPTH_MAX"
                            />

                            <field
                                    name="amount-start"
                                    type="number"
                                    min='0.01'
                                    default="0"
                                    readonly="false"
                                    label="PLG_ALFA_SHIPMENTS_STANDARD_FORM_SHIPMENT_AMOUNT_START"
                            />

                            <field
                                    name="amount-end"
                                    type="number"
                                    min='0.01'
                                    default="0"
                                    readonly="false"
                                    label="PLG_ALFA_SHIPMENTS_STANDARD_FORM_SHIPMENT_AMOUNT_END"
                            />

                            <field
                                    name="cost"
                                    type="number"
                                    min='0.01'
                                    default="0"
                                    readonly="false"
                                    label="PLG_ALFA_SHIPMENTS_STANDARD_FORM_SHIPMENT_COST"
                            />

                        </form>

                    </field>

                </form>

            </field>

            <!--
                Where a tracking number can be looked up, as a TEMPLATE rather
                than a stored URL. The number and the carrier live on the
                shipment row; only the endpoint is configuration, so when a
                carrier moves it one edit here repairs every order ever placed
                instead of leaving dead links on historic shipments.

                Placeholders: {tracking_number}, {carrier_name}
            -->
            <!--
                WHICH CHECKOUT FIELD CARRIES WHAT THIS CARRIER PRICES BY.

                The component holds no postcode concept and hardcodes no column:
                a postcode is a CARRIER's input, not the cart's, and a shop that
                delivers to lockers or collects in store has none at all. So the
                carrier says which field carries it, here, and reads the value
                off the cart at quote time.

                Leave a picker empty and that input is simply absent: the
                carrier is told "missing", not handed a zero that looks like an
                address. Cost rows whose band is unrestricted still match; rows
                with a real band do not.
            -->
            <field
                    name="postcode_field"
                    type="checkoutfield"
                    addfieldprefix="Alfa\Component\Alfa\Administrator\Field"
                    types="text"
                    sections="shipping,billing"
                    label="PLG_ALFA_SHIPMENTS_STANDARD_POSTCODE_FIELD_LABEL"
                    description="PLG_ALFA_SHIPMENTS_STANDARD_POSTCODE_FIELD_DESC"
            >
                <option value="">PLG_ALFA_SHIPMENTS_STANDARD_FIELD_NONE</option>
            </field>


            <field
                    name="tracking_url_template"
                    type="url"
                    filter="url"
                    label="PLG_ALFA_SHIPMENTS_STANDARD_TRACKING_URL_TEMPLATE"
                    description="PLG_ALFA_SHIPMENTS_STANDARD_TRACKING_URL_TEMPLATE_DESC"
                    hint="https://carrier.example/track?no={tracking_number}"
            />

            <!--
                Order-status automation map. Each shipment plugin declares ONLY
                the phases its lifecycle actually reaches, as fields named
                status_on_<status>. The core funnel (ShipmentLedger::update)
                reads these conventional keys from the method's params whenever
                a shipment status changes and runs the transition through
                Transition: stock, downloads, emails and activity log all fire
                from that single path. Empty = no automatic change (admin
                drives the order manually). The standard plugin reaches
                shipped / delivered / returned / cancelled via its admin
                actions and the shipment form.
            -->

            <field
                    name="status_on_shipped"
                    type="model"
                    model="orderstatuses"
                    column_value="id"
                    column_text="name"
                    orderBy="ordering"
                    label="PLG_ALFA_SHIPMENTS_STANDARD_STATUS_ON_SHIPPED_LABEL"
                    description="PLG_ALFA_SHIPMENTS_STANDARD_STATUS_ON_SHIPPED_DESC"
            >
                <option value="">PLG_ALFA_SHIPMENTS_STANDARD_STATUS_NO_CHANGE</option>
            </field>

            <field
                    name="status_on_delivered"
                    type="model"
                    model="orderstatuses"
                    column_value="id"
                    column_text="name"
                    orderBy="ordering"
                    label="PLG_ALFA_SHIPMENTS_STANDARD_STATUS_ON_DELIVERED_LABEL"
                    description="PLG_ALFA_SHIPMENTS_STANDARD_STATUS_ON_DELIVERED_DESC"
            >
                <option value="">PLG_ALFA_SHIPMENTS_STANDARD_STATUS_NO_CHANGE</option>
            </field>

            <field
                    name="status_on_returned"
                    type="model"
                    model="orderstatuses"
                    column_value="id"
                    column_text="name"
                    orderBy="ordering"
                    label="PLG_ALFA_SHIPMENTS_STANDARD_STATUS_ON_RETURNED_LABEL"
                    description="PLG_ALFA_SHIPMENTS_STANDARD_STATUS_ON_RETURNED_DESC"
            >
                <option value="">PLG_ALFA_SHIPMENTS_STANDARD_STATUS_NO_CHANGE</option>
            </field>

            <field
                    name="status_on_cancelled"
                    type="model"
                    model="orderstatuses"
                    column_value="id"
                    column_text="name"
                    orderBy="ordering"
                    label="PLG_ALFA_SHIPMENTS_STANDARD_STATUS_ON_CANCELLED_LABEL"
                    description="PLG_ALFA_SHIPMENTS_STANDARD_STATUS_ON_CANCELLED_DESC"
            >
                <option value="">PLG_ALFA_SHIPMENTS_STANDARD_STATUS_NO_CHANGE</option>
            </field>
        </fieldset>
    </fields>
</form>